From 8f7f5f523be28af284e8dc09edcdcd111935d007 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claudecode <hockinglee@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 18:09:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] build: drop the git2 dependency from build metadata

`shadow-rs` stamps build information into `--version`, and its default features
pull in `git2`, and with it `libgit2-sys`, to read the branch and commit hash
out of the repository. That is the only thing a clipboard manager wanted a git
library for: it is a build-time dependency, never linked into the binaries that
ship, and building from a release tarball leaves those two fields empty anyway
because there is no repository to read.

Turning the feature off removes 28 crates from the graph, among them
`libgit2-sys`, which compiles roughly ten megabytes of C for the build script,
and `libz-sys`, `url` and the ICU stack behind it. `shadow-rs` falls back to the
`git` command, so a build made inside a checkout still reports its branch and
commit; a build from a tarball reports what it reported before.

It also means a packaged build no longer has to be reconciled with whichever
libgit2 the distribution ships.
---
 Cargo.lock | 295 -----------------------------------------------------
 Cargo.toml |   2 +-
 2 files changed, 1 insertion(+), 296 deletions(-)

